      "page_level_design_instruction": "The Clearmind Therapy Home page is a classic stacked landing layout rendered through a bento modular lens \u2014 every section uses rounded, card-based modules, asymmetric grid arrangements, and a disciplined color system to create warmth without clinical coldness. The overall page background is Clearmind Cloud (#F5F7FA), which acts as the continuous canvas tying all sections together. Individual bento modules alternate between Clearmind White (#FFFFFF) for elevated card surfaces, Clearmind Mist (#E8EEF4) for secondary panels, and Clearmind Dew (#D6F0E8) for accent-tinted highlight tiles. Clearmind Slate (#1A2332) anchors all primary headings and navigation. Clearmind Sage (#4AAE8C) is the single bright accent \u2014 used exclusively for primary CTAs, active underlines, icon fills, and key stat highlights to maintain visual focus. Clearmind Stone (#6B7A8F) handles all secondary text, captions, eyebrow labels, and meta copy. Clearmind Coral (#E8715A) appears only as a rare warmth accent \u2014 perhaps a single decorative dot or a subtle badge in the testimonial section.\n\nTypography follows the shared system strictly: Manrope 700\u2013800 for all headings with tight letter-spacing (-0.02em), Source Sans 3 400 at 1.7 line-height for all body and description copy, and DM Sans 500 in small uppercase with 0.10em letter-spacing for all eyebrow labels and stat captions. The heading scale steps down cleanly from a large display size in the hero (clamp 48\u201372px) through H2 section headers (36\u201348px) to H3 card titles (20\u201324px).\n\nSection rhythm is deliberately varied to prevent monotony: the hero is full-width and visually generous with a split layout; the stats section is compact and horizontally dense; the feature grid opens into an asymmetric bento arrangement; the testimonial section returns to a three-column card rhythm; and the closing CTA is bold and centered. Vertical spacing between sections uses consistent padding (80\u2013100px top/bottom on desktop, 56px on tablet, 40px on mobile) with no section bleeding into the next \u2014 each section is visually self-contained but connected by the shared Cloud background.\n\nOn desktop (\u22651280px), the layout uses a 12-column grid at 1200px max-width with 24px gutters. On tablet (768\u20131279px), it collapses to 8 columns with card grids moving to 2-column arrangements. On mobile (\u2264767px), everything stacks to a single column with full-width cards, reduced heading sizes, and vertically stacked CTAs. Bento modules maintain their rounded-corner radius (16px on large cards, 12px on smaller tiles) at all breakpoints. No section uses a full-bleed dark background except the closing CTA, which uses Clearmind Slate as its background surface for maximum contrast and visual weight as the page's final statement.",
      "section_design_plans": [
        {
          "id": "home-section-1",
          "nl_prompt": "Design a split-layout hero section on a Clearmind Cloud (#F5F7FA) background with a maximum width of 1200px centered on the page and 100px vertical padding top and bottom. The left column (roughly 55% width on desktop) contains all text content stacked vertically with generous spacing. Begin with the eyebrow label 'Mental Health Therapy' rendered in DM Sans 500, uppercase, 11px, 0.10em letter-spacing, Clearmind Sage (#4AAE8C) color, with a 2px Sage left-border accent or a small Sage pill badge. Below it, place the headline 'You deserve a space that feels like yours.' in Manrope 800, approximately 60px on desktop (clamp to 36px on mobile), Clearmind Slate (#1A2332), tight letter-spacing (-0.03em), line-height 1.15, spanning no more than 10 words per line for impact. Below the headline, render the subheadline 'Clearmind Therapy connects you with licensed therapists who meet you where you are \u2014 and help you move forward.' in Source Sans 3 400, 18px, Clearmind Stone (#6B7A8F), line-height 1.7, capped at 52 characters per line. Below the subheadline, place two CTA buttons side by side with 16px gap: the primary button 'Find Your Therapist' uses a solid Clearmind Sage (#4AAE8C) fill with Clearmind White text in DM Sans 500 14px uppercase, 8px vertical padding, 24px horizontal padding, 10px border-radius, and a subtle hover darkening; the secondary button 'Explore Our Services' uses a transparent fill with a 1.5px Clearmind Slate border and Clearmind Slate text, same sizing, with a hover fill of Clearmind Mist. On the right column (45% width), position the illustration asset: a calm, modular bento-style arrangement of soft geometric shapes \u2014 overlapping rounded rectangles in Clearmind Dew (#D6F0E8), Clearmind Mist (#E8EEF4), and Clearmind White \u2014 suggesting an open window, a potted plant silhouette, and a comfortable chair without literal depiction. The illustration is contained within a large rounded rectangle module (24px radius) in Clearmind White with a soft box-shadow (0 4px 24px rgba(26,35,50,0.07)) that floats slightly above the background. The illustration fills the right column from roughly 40px below the nav to the bottom of the section. On tablet, the layout shifts to stacked: illustration moves above the text block, constrained to 400px max-height. On mobile, the illustration is hidden or reduced to a decorative top banner strip at 120px height to preserve reading space."
